--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The package contents:
bin/ - the folder with simlinks to all binary files
extra/ - external packages such as kyotocabinet, snappy, LiteRed, fermat
usr/ - the folder where the external libraries are installed
temp/ - temporary folder, not included in git
sources/ - the sources of C++ FIRE
poly/ - where polynomial version of FIRE is built
prime/ - where modular arithmetic version of FIRE is built
examples/ - examples
documentation/ - the folder where documentation is generated
tests/ - the folder where all tests used by tests.makefile reside
reports/ - the folder where reports can be stored, not logged by git
reconstruction/ - the folder where reconstruction programs reside
tests.makefile - Makefile which describes tests to be run on FIRE

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

For Mac OS X users
    
To configure and make a project:

    ./configure --cpp=g++ --cc=gcc
    make dep
    make

Troubleshooting:
  
    error: "fatal error: 'omp.h' file not found" with clang, while gcc is ok
    fix: sudo apt install libomp-dev
 
    error: unsupported option '-fopenmp'
    fix: Occurs when clang compiler is used even
         though you have chosen a gcc/g++ in 
         configure options.
         To fix this error you have to write an
         aliases for gcc in your shell .*rc file
         Also you have to install gcc/g++.

         Example:
            1.  Run the command in terminal:
                brew install gcc@12
            2a. If you are using bash:
                    vim ~/.bashrc
            2b. If you are using zsh:
                    vim ~/.zshrc
            3.  add this text to the end of the file:
                    alias gcc='gcc-12'
                    alias cc='gcc-12'
                    alias g++='g++-12'
                    alias c++='g++-12'

         Now try making FIRE again after those commands:
            make depclean
            make clean
            
